From 03b34134d5e50ca0e82260c28f405fc993245e30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:58:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09736/11362] [outer-loop] Attempt manifest names the loaded
 model, not the frozen pin (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6690)

Found while verifying per-attempt retention on a live tu93 run. The archive
manifest recorded "model": "Qwen3.5-9B-MTP" while the run had actually loaded
Qwen3.8-27B-Q4_K_M.gguf via CARNOT_ARC_GGUF_PATH.

Both archive sites passed `str(self.repo_substr)` -- the harness's frozen pin,
which is our INTENT, not what loaded. `_effective_model_label()` already exists
for exactly this and is used by `generator_model_declared`; it prefers
`model_path` when the override is set. The archive sites simply bypassed it.

This matters more here than in a log line: the manifest is the durable
provenance record for retained attempts, so a wrong label misattributes every
archived model to a model that never ran. REQ-ARC-WMTE-6670 exists because that
same mislabel "misdirected a whole investigation" during the supab5 A/B.

Evidence: 2 tests (SCENARIO-ARC-WMTE-6690-7) covering the override and the
no-override fallback. Mutation-proved -- reverting both sites to `repo_substr`
turns the override test RED with the exact live-observed
['Qwen3.5-9B-MTP', 'Qwen3.5-9B-MTP'], then GREEN on restore. 16 pass, ruff clean.

The tests reached HEAD ahead of this fix: conductor checkpoint d5425c44b2 swept
the in-flight test file at 16:56:58, leaving HEAD momentarily RED. This commit
closes that window. Canonical world_model.py write path untouched.

Two test-suite-mutation markers deleted deliberately, per the guard's own
instruction for an intended change. Both were armed by CONCURRENT agents' pytest
runs at 20:57:00Z and 20:57:01Z, both named only this file, and both listed it
`unattributed` -- i.e. neither run was observed writing it. The content is this
authored 2-line edit, confirmed by diffing against HEAD before deleting. This is
the documented over-report, not test damage; `git checkout --` here would have
destroyed authored work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
---
 python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py b/python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py
index 52bd4873d5..2956df7cfd 100644
--- a/python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py
+++ b/python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py
@@ -7989,7 +7989,7 @@ class LocalGGUFProposer:
             (E3_DIR / game / "world_model.py").write_text(code)
             # REQ-ARC-WMTE-6690: retain this attempt; the canonical write above is unchanged.
             self.last_attempt_archive = _archive_engine_attempt(
-                game, code, writer="gen_to_file", model=str(self.repo_substr)
+                game, code, writer="gen_to_file", model=self._effective_model_label()
             )
             return True, "local gguf (GPU server) wrote world_model.py"
         return False, code
@@ -8005,7 +8005,7 @@ class LocalGGUFProposer:
         (E3_DIR / game / "world_model.py").write_text(code)
         # REQ-ARC-WMTE-6690: retain this attempt; the canonical write above is unchanged.
         self.last_attempt_archive = _archive_engine_attempt(
-            game, code, writer="write_world_model", model=str(self.repo_substr), note=note
+            game, code, writer="write_world_model", model=self._effective_model_label(), note=note
         )
         msg = "local gguf (GPU server) wrote world_model.py"
         return True, (f"{msg} ({note})" if note else msg)
